/*
:name: type_bound_generic_port
:type: warning
:warning: is not a compile-time value
:help: resolved only on a variable declaration inside the body
*/

// 2f-type_bound — KNOWN GAP, pinned deliberately as a warning.
//
// A generic width resolves on a variable declaration inside the body, because
// prp2lnast can emit the `bits=` -> max/min desugar as statements just before
// the declaration. A PORT type slot has no statement position, so the bound
// cannot be deferred there and the port is left unbounded (`input a`, one bit).
//
// That is a real defect, but it PRE-DATES the deferral work and turning it into
// a hard error would reject code that used to compile. So it warns: the drop is
// no longer silent, and this fixture is what will notice when the gap closes --
// at which point this becomes an `:type: compile` fixture asserting the port is
// eight bits wide.

mod m<N=8>(a:unsigned(bits=N)) -> (y:u8@[]) { // locate_warning_here
  y = a
}
pub mod top(a:u8) -> (y:u8@[]) {
  y = m<N=8>(a=a)
}
